# HITL edit test flow (note-edit baseline)

Use this flow when validating **M8 note edit** on hardware. Serial capture is mandatory for a verified run.

## Build

Flash **`teensy41-capture-serial`** (not plain `teensy41`) so `#CAP` / `REVT` / `ST` and edit log lines appear on USB serial:

```bash
pio run -e teensy41-capture-serial -t upload
```

## Canonical test command

1. Start external capture in one terminal:

```bash
.venv/bin/python scripts/capture_session.py --port /dev/cu.usbmodem154944801
```

2. Run the edit baseline in another terminal (from project root):

```bash
.venv/bin/python scripts/host_midi_automation_edit_baseline.py \
  --midi-out "Teensy" --midi-in "Teensy" \
  --serial-port /dev/cu.usbmodem154944801 \
  --track 5 --midi-channel 5 \
  --record-bars 2 \
  --start-transport \
  --phase-wait-ms 500 --final-wait-ms 3000 --press-ms 120 \
  --undo-redo-delay-ms 3000
```

3. Stop capture with Ctrl+C.

4. Re-verify from the saved log if needed:

```bash
.venv/bin/python scripts/host_midi_automation_edit_baseline.py \
  ...same args... \
  --verify-serial-log captures/<session>.log
```

(`--serial-port` can be omitted when using `--verify-serial-log` only.)

## Required pass criteria (M8)

With default **`--require-m8-pass-verify`** (on):

- Record prelude completes (fixture `REVT` count matches fixture notes).
- Edit session markers present (`entered note edit mode`, `Created 32nd note`, `Deleting note`, `POSITION EDIT`, `exited edit mode`, …).
- **Exactly one** `NoteEditSessionCommitted` between enter and exit edit.
- In-edit undo/redo (default on): `NoteEditSession undo` and `NoteEditSession redo` in serial.
- Post-exit undo/redo (default on): `Note edit pass undone` after exit; redo via `Overdub redone`.
- Move/display / overlap checks pass for the standard fixture (see script report `issues`).

Use `--no-m8-pass-verify` only for pre-M8 capture replay. **`--require-m8-span-verify`** is a deprecated alias for **`--require-m8-pass-verify`**.

